  "output_text": "{\"action\":\"answer\",\"expression\":\"\",\"queries\":[],\"pages\":[189],\"status\":\"answered\",\"answer\":\"The report does not prescribe an itemized capital budget or recurring annual operating cost for a first domestic IXP. It only characterizes IXP development costs as “relatively modest” and notes they may be supportable in nascent markets if the sector is not monopolistic.\",\"citations\":[{\"page\":189,\"region_label\":\"Strengthening data infrastructure, paragraph beginning “The economic case for domestic data infrastructure”\",\"bbox\":[0.454,0.514,0.802,0.906],\"quote\":\"The cost of developing IXPs is relatively modest and likely can be supported even in nascent markets so long as the sector is not monopolistic.\"}]}",
